title": "Montreal", "exists": 1, "page_title": "Montreal", "lat": 45.50888889, "lon": -73.55416667, "image_file": "Montreal, Quebec skyline.jpg", "extract": "Montreal (French: Montréal) is the largest city in the province of Quebec, the second-largest in Canada, and the eighth-largest in North America. Founded in 1642 as Ville-Marie, or \"City of Mary\", it now takes its name from Mount Royal, the triple-peaked mountain around which the early settlement was built. The city is centred on the Island of Montreal and several much smaller, peripheral islands, the largest of which is Île Bizard.", "wikidata": "Q340"}}}